# Docs And Config Standards

- Keep PRD and implementation docs actionable: each feature needs scope, data model, command/API/UI behavior, gate, rollback, and test expectation.
- Avoid vague placeholders such as TBD, later, proper handling, or appropriate validation.
- Config files should be human-editable YAML with stable IDs and explicit defaults.
- Do not store secrets in config. Reference a secret name or local secret provider instead.
- When documenting network behavior, distinguish target architecture, current fact, temporary offline, and evidence gap.
- Every operational claim should cite a path or generated evidence ID.
- Update docs when changing status names, gate behavior, automation modes, or directory conventions.
